```rust
// A chain of references that couples struct lifetimes all the way up
struct FileRef<'a> { content: &'a str }
struct Parser<'a> { file: FileRef<'a> }
struct Compiler<'a> { parser: Parser<'a> }
```

fix:
Clones the short-lived data or use thread-safe shared references like `Arc<str>` or `String` to take explicit ownership.
```rust
struct FileData { content: String }
struct Parser { file: FileData }
struct Compiler { parser: Parser }
```
